# NEVER commit a key. contracts/.env holds the deployer private key; the game's
# own .env holds the two server signing keys. Both are real money on mainnet.
.env
# Every .env VARIANT too, not just the bare name. `deploy.mjs --chain
# robinhood-fork` writes .env.fork, and a rehearsal generates real signer
# private keys into it exactly like a real deploy does. A rule that only
# covered `.env` left three keys sitting untracked, one `git add -A` from
# being published.
.env.*
!.env.example
# A rehearsal's addresses are predictions, not a deployment. Keeping them
# here would put a file that looks exactly like a deployment record next to
# the real ones.
stockmonsters-mmo/deployments/*-fork.json
contracts/.env
stockmonsters-mmo/.env
new-assets/
workadventure-master/
